CrossBible, generic package (noarch)
====================================

This package is for every Linux and every processor that has the .NET runtime, version 11 or later (https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download).
The program is not compiled for a processor: it is the .NET program, and it runs on the runtime of your system. (The packages for Debian, Fedora,
Arch Linux and Alpine hold the same program compiled to machine code, and need no runtime: use them when there is one for your system.)

Install:

    tar -xzf crossbible-<version>-noarch.tar.gz
    cd crossbible-<version>-noarch
    sudo ./install.sh              (into /usr/local)
    ./install.sh --user            (into ~/.local, no root needed)
    ./install.sh --prefix /opt/cb  (into another folder)

Remove: the same command with --uninstall (and the same --user or --prefix).

Without installing: dotnet crossbible/CrossBible.Desktop.dll

It needs, as every desktop program on Linux: X11 (libX11, libICE, libSM), fontconfig and a font, OpenGL (libGL), ICU (libicu), OpenSSL and zlib.
